{ Black has as many as six (!) thematic breaks in the Hippopotamus. Let’s have another look at the standard set-up:

The central breaks ...e6-e5/...d6-d5 will normally be a defensive reaction to the enemy invasion.

On the other hand, the breaks ...g6-g5/...f7-f5/...c7-c5/...b6-b5 are active attempts at gaining counterplay.

You will normally focus on only one or two of these. In real games it happens that White mistakenly provokes advances that are good for Black, and vice versa. } { [%cal Ge6e5,Gd6d5,Rg6g5,Rf7f5,Rc7c5,Rb6b5] }
 *


