1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 Nf6 3. d3 e6 4. Nd2 b6 5. b3 Bb7 6. Bb2 Nbd7 7. e3 { [White's pawn structure is unique to the Hippopotamus Opening. Here the first player has not been challenged for his passive layout, but he must soon find a way to contest the center.] } 7... Bd6 8. Ne2 Qe7 9. a3 O-O-O!? $13 { [Provocative, but the position offers equal chances.] } 10. b4 e5 11. c3?! (11. c4 $13 { is much better. }) 11... c5 (11... h5! $17 { White has to be careful. }) 12. d4 exd4 13. cxd4 c4 14. b5 (14. Nc3 $13 { is more flexible. }) 14... Rhe8?! (14... h5 $15 { is still best. }) 15. Nc3 h5 16. O-O h4 17. a4 hxg3 18. hxg3 Bxg3?! (18... Bc7 $13 { followed by ...Kb8 takes time to consolidate. } { [%cal Yc8b8] }) 19. Qf3!? (19. fxg3 Qxe3+ 20. Rf2 Qxg3 21. Nf1 $14 { is interesting. }) 19... Bc7 (19... Bd6?! { because of } 20. Nxc4 $14) 20. Nxc4? (20. Ba3 Bd6 (20... Qe6? 21. Bh3 $18) (20... Ne5? { fails to } 21. Qh3+! Qd7 22. dxe5 $16 { etc. }) 21. Bxd6 Qxd6 22. Nxc4 Qc7 23. Nd2 $14 { with a good game. }) 20... Rh8!? $15 (20... Qb4? 21. Rfc1 $16 { and so forth. }) (20... Kb8! $17 { or even 20...g5!?, and Black's attack looks faster. }) 21. Rfc1 Ne4? (21... Kb8 { and if } 22. a5 { the disruptive } 22... Qb4! 23. Ra4 Qb3 24. a6 Ba8 25. Ba3 Ne4 $15 { gives Black the better game. }) 22. Ba3?! $16 (22. Nxe4 dxe4 23. Qxf7 $18 { winning. }) 22... Qe6?! (22... Qh4 $16 { is a little better, but White has a clear advantage. }) 23. Nxe4 dxe4 24. Nd6+ $18 { [White is winning.] } 24... Kb8 (24... Qxd6 25. Bxd6 exf3 26. Rxc7+ Kb8 27. Rxb7+ $18 { wins. }) 25. Qxf7 Qg4 26. Rxc7 Kxc7 27. Nxb7 Rdf8 (27... Kxb7 { then } 28. Qd5+ $18 { and wins. }) 28. Bd6+ Kxb7 29. Qd5+ Kc8 30. Qa8+ Nb8 31. Qxb8+ Kd7 32. Qc7+ Ke6 33. Qe7+ Kd5 34. Qe5+ Kc4 35. Bxf8 Rxf8 36. Qxe4 Qxe4 37. Bxe4 { 1-0 White wins. } 1-0


